error[E0432]: the template of `format` must be a string literal
  --> tests/programs/m48/e0432.la:3:20
  |
3 |     let a = format(t, 1);
  |                    ^
  |
  = help: write `format("{} and {:>5}", a, b)`: one `{}` or `{:spec}` per value

error[E0432]: the template has 2 holes but 1 value follows
  --> tests/programs/m48/e0432.la:4:20
  |
4 |     let b = format("{} and {}", 1);
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: write `format("{} and {:>5}", a, b)`: one `{}` or `{:spec}` per value

error[E0432]: `{x}` in a template: holes are `{}` or `{:spec}`, filled from the arguments in order
  --> tests/programs/m48/e0432.la:5:20
  |
5 |     let c = format("{x}", 1);
  |                    ^^^^^
  |
  = help: write `format("{} and {:>5}", a, b)`: one `{}` or `{:spec}` per value

error[E0431]: `q` isn't a format: use `x`, `X`, `b` or `o`
  --> tests/programs/m48/e0432.la:6:22
  |
6 |     let d = format("{:q}", 1);
  |                      ^^
  |
  = help: a specifier is `[[fill]align][#][0][width][.precision][kind]`, e.g. `{x:>8.2}`

For more about E0432 and E0431, run `lughac explain <code>`.
